{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.lambda_inviscid_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.lambda_inviscid_identity","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/hyperbolic-overlap-saturation.lean#L117-L125","doc":"**High-Reynolds inviscid-limit identity.**  In the limit\n$\\nu \\to 0$ at fixed $\\Gamma, \\pi$, $\\lambda \\cdot (2\\Gamma) =\n\\pi\\nu$, so $\\lambda \\sim \\pi\\nu/(2\\Gamma)$ — i.e. *half* the\nquasi-steady answer $\\pi\\nu/\\Gamma$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.kappa_squared_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.kappa_squared_pos","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/hyperbolic-overlap-saturation.lean#L104-L115","doc":"**Strict positivity of the squared core aspect ratio.**  The\ncorrected asymptotic ratio $\\kappa^2 = \\lambda$ is strictly\npositive: the cores lock into a finite elliptical profile.  The\nnumerical value is $\\pi\\nu/(2\\Gamma + \\pi\\nu)$, not\n$\\pi\\nu/\\Gamma$.  (Re-scoped 2026-10-13: $\\kappa^2$ is the core\naspect ratio, not a Levi condition number, and its positivity is no\nlonger read as branch (A) of `conj:levi-degeneracy`, which is\nwithdrawn.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.lambda_lt_quasi_steady","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.lambda_lt_quasi_steady","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/hyperbolic-overlap-saturation.lean#L91-L102","doc":"**The quasi-steady value overstates.**  For any positive\nparameters, $\\lambda < \\lambda_{\\mathrm{QS}}$ — i.e. the user\nconstant $\\pi\\nu/\\Gamma$ overestimates the true asymptotic\nratio by the factor $1 + \\pi\\nu/(2\\Gamma)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.lambda_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.lambda_pos","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/hyperbolic-overlap-saturation.lean#L81-L89","doc":"**Positivity of the corrected ratio.**  $\\lambda > 0$ whenever\n$\\nu, \\Gamma, \\pi > 0$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.proportionality_balance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.proportionality_balance","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/hyperbolic-overlap-saturation.lean#L70-L79","doc":"**The proportionality balance.**  If $V_2(t) = \\lambda\\,V_1(t)$\nand $V_1$ grows linearly with rate $b$, the Townsend ODE for\n$V_2$ forces $\\lambda\\,b = -(2\\Gamma/\\pi)\\,\\lambda + 2\\nu$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.lambdaQuasiSteady","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.lambdaQuasiSteady","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/hyperbolic-overlap-saturation.lean#L66-L68","doc":"The quasi-steady (incorrect) value $\\lambda_{\\mathrm{QS}} =\n\\pi\\nu/\\Gamma$ obtained by setting $\\dot V_2 = 0$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.lambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.lambda","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/hyperbolic-overlap-saturation.lean#L61-L64","doc":"The corrected asymptotic proportionality ratio\n$\\lambda = \\pi\\nu/(2\\Gamma + \\pi\\nu)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.HyperbolicOverlapSaturation.b","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/hyperbolic-overlap-saturation.lean#L57-L59","doc":"Linear growth rate of $V_1$ in the saturated regime:\n$b = 2\\Gamma/\\pi + 2\\nu$. ","signatureChunk":0}]}